// Template for an IW4 x64 zone definition.
//
// Rename this file to <project>.zone before adding it to the build. The
// Linker selects a definition from the target name and looks for
// <target>.zone on its source search path. There is no name inside the
// definition that establishes that relationship, so the filename is
// part of the build interface.
//
// IW4MS names the retail Microsoft Store/GDK x64 variant of Modern
// Warfare 2. Its asset data is IW4 data, but its fastfiles contain
// 8-byte serialized pointers. This is why the Linker treats it as a
// separate game and why an x64 Linker build is required.
//
// Note that >game,IW4 is not interchangeable with >game,IW4MS here. It
// selects the 32-bit IW4 fastfile format and the x64 game will reject
// the result.
//
>game,IW4MS

// By default the output fastfile takes its name from this definition.
// Use
// >name when the build target and the name written to disk need to
// differ. A common case is a project that deliberately produces the
// name of a stock zone so that the installed fastfile replaces it.
//
// >name,TEMPLATE

// Assets are written one per line as <type>,<name>. The type tells the
// Linker which asset loader to use and the name is interpreted
// according to that loader.
//
// There is one small syntax detail worth calling out here. An empty
// field between the type and name marks the asset as a reference. The
// asset is then expected to come from a zone already loaded by the game
// and is not serialized into this fastfile.
//
// For example:
//
//   material,mc/mtl_example     writes mc/mtl_example into this fastfile
//   material,,mc/mtl_example    records a reference to the loaded material
//
// Note that the spelling of an asset name is type-specific. Some asset
// types include a directory component in the name and some do not. See
// ../README.md for the naming rule and the source directory used by
// each type.
//
// localize,TEMPLATE
// techniqueset,,2d
// image,example_image
// material,example_material
// xmodel,example_model
// rawfile,common_scripts/example.gsc
// menu,example_menu
// menulist,ui/example_menus.txt

// A definition can contain directives in addition to asset entries.
//
// include expands another zone definition at this point and brings its
// assets into this zone.
//
// include,other_project

// ignore tells the Linker that another zone already provides those
// assets. They are left out of this fastfile, which is how a zone can
// depend on content that the game is expected to have loaded already.
//
// ignore,common_mp

// build names another zone target that belongs to the same project. The
// Linker builds that target as part of processing this definition.
//
// build,TEMPLATE_extra

// >gdt loads a GDT by name. The lookup uses the Linker's GDT search
// path. source_data/ is the default tree in this project.
//
// >gdt,example
